{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5419) to implement `cmd/factor` for the go-unix-utils project. The specific scope is srd065-factor requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (core factorization behavior only). Two files must be created: `cmd/factor/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` (differential tests against `gfactor`). The acceptance criteria require: successful build, clean `go vet`, passing tests (or graceful skip), and all four R1.x requirements exercised by differential tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Prime factorization via trial division (sufficient for int64 range per non_goals)\n   - GNU factor output format: `NUMBER: FACTOR FACTOR ...` (ascending order, repeated for multiplicity)\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU `gfactor` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`, `BuildBinary`, `DiffTest` struct for test cases\n   - Graceful skip when reference binary not in PATH (`exec.LookPath` + `t.Skip`)\n   - 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit, SPDX copyright header required\n   - Write all files before building/testing (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd065-factor.yaml` (READ)\n     - Contains full SRD for factor utility\n     - R1 (Core factorization): R1.1 format output, R1.2 handle 1, R1.3 handle primes, R1.4 multiple arguments\n     - R2 (Stdin mode): R2.1 read stdin when no args, R2.2 int64 max, R2.3 skip blank lines, R2.4 error on invalid input\n     - R3 (Help/version): R3.1 --help, R3.2 --version, R3.3 stdout output, R3.4 stderr errors\n     - R4 (Exit codes/testing): R4.1 exit 0 on success, R4.2 exit 1 on invalid, R4.3 diff tests, R4.4 test coverage list\n     - Non-goals: no arbitrary precision beyond int64, no advanced algorithms (trial division suffices)\n   - `cmd/factor/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Factor implementation with SIGPIPE handler, argument processing, trial division factorization\n   - `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using `testutils.RunDiffTests` against `gfactor`\n   - Key existing code patterns referenced (from project_context source_code):\n     - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must call at start of main\n     - `pkg/testutils/build.go`: `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles cmd package for testing\n     - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`: `DiffTest` struct and `RunDiffTests` function\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. No code has been written. Only the SRD file was read.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Determined the precise scope: only R1.1-R1.4 (core factorization behavior), not the full SRD. The task title \"[stitch] cmd/factor: srd065 R1.1-R1.4\" and requirements section both confirm this scope.\n   - However, to make a testable binary, the implementation needs a functional main() with argument processing, which touches R1.4 (multiple arguments) and implicitly requires basic stdin support or argument iteration.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive stitch task prompt with full project context, SRDs, source code, constitutions, and task description for implementing cmd/factor with requirements R1.1-R1.4\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/factor/main.go` with prime factorization implementation\n   - Create `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` with differential tests against gfactor\n   - Run `go build -o bin/factor ./cmd/factor/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/factor/...` to check for warnings\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/factor/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd065-factor.yaml`) to understand requirements R1.1-R1.4. I was at the planning stage, about to implement the two files. No code has been written yet.\n\n   The four requirements to implement are:\n   - R1.1: Format output as `NUMBER: FACTOR FACTOR ...` with ascending factors and multiplicity\n   - R1.2: Special case for 1: print `1:` with no factors\n   - R1.3: Prime numbers print as `NUMBER: NUMBER` (sole factor)\n   - R1.4: Multiple arguments processed in order, one line each\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/factor/main.go` and `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` in a single pass, then build and test. The implementation needs:\n   - main.go: copyright header, package main, imports (fmt, os, strconv, math, bufio, pkg/sys), InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), argument iteration, trial division factorization producing `NUMBER: FACTOR FACTOR ...` format, stdin fallback for no-args case (needed for a functional binary even though R2 isn't in scope)\n   - factor_test.go: copyright header, TestDiff function with BuildBinary, LookPath(\"gfactor\"), DiffTest cases covering single number (12→\"12: 2 2 3\"), number 1 (\"1:\"), prime (97→\"97: 97\"), multiple arguments, and RunDiffTests call\n\n   This directly continues the task from the prompt: \"Follow these steps in order... 3. Implement — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5419/8d6177a1-d4e9-4a11-91e1-eb5cf1509335.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resu