{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LoNnCgctWD1WuJH1AP53Dz","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information requested. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully explored the repository and found the key patterns you requested. Here are the three core components:\n\n### 1. Simple cmd/main.go Example: `cmd/true/main.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/cmd/true/main.go`\n\n**Structure:**\n- Copyright header (2026 Petar Djukic, MIT license)\n- Package documentation with specification reference (srd013-true R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2)\n- Imports: `fmt`, `os`, and `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n- Help and version text constants\n- SIGPIPE handler: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at the start of main()\n- Argument parsing with `--help` and `--version` flags, with error handling for write failures (`os.Exit(1)` on fmt.Fprint error)\n- Simple early exit pattern with no explicit exit code at end (defaults to 0 on success)\n\nAnother example (`cmd/false/main.go`) shows the inverse pattern - exits with 1 instead of 0, and omits error checking on fmt.Fprint for help/version (just calls Fprint and then Exit).\n\n### 2. Test File Example: `cmd/true/true_test.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/cmd/true/true_test.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses differential testing: compares Go implementation against GNU reference binary\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles the Go implementation from current directory\n- `exec.LookPath(\"gtrue\")` - finds reference binary (GNU true with 'g' prefix), skips test if not found\n- `testutils.NormalizeFunc` - custom normalizer function (discards stdout for help/version output)\n- `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: `Name`, `Args`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize` (array of NormalizeFunc)\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` - runs all tests as subtests, comparing outputs\n\n### 3. Test Utilities: `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**DiffTest struct fields** (R1.1-R1.4):\n- `Name string` - subtest identifier\n- `Args []string` - command-line arguments\n- `Stdin []byte` - input data (nil = EOF immediately, empty = open then close)\n- `Env []string` - environment overrides (merged with inherited env + LC_ALL=C)\n- `WorkDir string` - working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n- `ExitCode int` - expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize []NormalizeFunc` - slice of normalization functions applied in order\n- `ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte` - file assertions (optional)\n\n**RunDiffTests signature** (R2.1):\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\nRuns each test as a named subtest, executes both binaries with identical inputs, applies normalizers in order to stdout/stderr of both, and compares outputs.\n\n**Additional utilities:**\n- `NormalizeFunc` - type alias for `func([]byte) []byte`\n- `TimestampNormalizer` - built-in normalizer for timestamp patterns\n- `ComposeNormalizers` - helper to chain multiple normalizers\n- `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string)` - compiles Go package and returns binary path (placed in t.TempDir())\n\n### SIGPIPE Handler Pattern: `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\nImplementation uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel (not `signal.Ignore`):\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\nMatches GNU coreutils behavior - exits with 0 when stdout/stderr is closed. Safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d6177a1-d4e9-4a11-91e1-eb5cf1509335","uuid":"bd1a9d05-94fd-4af3-bf1e-c3f653418711","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:23:26.080Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419, I need to see:\n\n1. An existing cmd/ main.go that's simple (like cmd/yes or cmd/true or cmd/basename) - read the full file to see the copyright header, imports, SIGPIPE handler pattern, and overall structure.\n2. An existing cmd/ test file (like cmd/yes/yes_test.go or cmd/basename/basename_test.go) - read the full file to see the differential test pattern with BuildBinary, LookPath, DiffTest struct usage, and RunDiffTests.\n3. Read pkg/testutils/difftest.go to see the DiffTest struct fields and RunDiffTests signature.\n\nFirst glob for cmd/*/main.go to find what exists, pick a simple one, and read it plus its test file. Then read the testutils file.","agentId":"aa4436b6fe0907359","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information requested. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully explored the repository and found the key patterns you requested. Here are the three core components:\n\n### 1. Simple cmd/main.go Example: `cmd/true/main.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/cmd/true/main.go`\n\n**Structure:**\n- Copyright header (2026 Petar Djukic, MIT license)\n- Package documentation with specification reference (srd013-true R1.1-R1.3, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2)\n- Imports: `fmt`, `os`, and `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n- Help and version text constants\n- SIGPIPE handler: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` called at the start of main()\n- Argument parsing with `--help` and `--version` flags, with error handling for write failures (`os.Exit(1)` on fmt.Fprint error)\n- Simple early exit pattern with no explicit exit code at end (defaults to 0 on success)\n\nAnother example (`cmd/false/main.go`) shows the inverse pattern - exits with 1 instead of 0, and omits error checking on fmt.Fprint for help/version (just calls Fprint and then Exit).\n\n### 2. Test File Example: `cmd/true/true_test.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/cmd/true/true_test.go`\n\n**Pattern:**\n- Uses differential testing: compares Go implementation against GNU reference binary\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles the Go implementation from current directory\n- `exec.LookPath(\"gtrue\")` - finds reference binary (GNU true with 'g' prefix), skips test if not found\n- `testutils.NormalizeFunc` - custom normalizer function (discards stdout for help/version output)\n- `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: `Name`, `Args`, `ExitCode`, `Normalize` (array of NormalizeFunc)\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` - runs all tests as subtests, comparing outputs\n\n### 3. Test Utilities: `pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n\n**DiffTest struct fields** (R1.1-R1.4):\n- `Name string` - subtest identifier\n- `Args []string` - command-line arguments\n- `Stdin []byte` - input data (nil = EOF immediately, empty = open then close)\n- `Env []string` - environment overrides (merged with inherited env + LC_ALL=C)\n- `WorkDir string` - working directory (defaults to t.TempDir())\n- `ExitCode int` - expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize []NormalizeFunc` - slice of normalization functions applied in order\n- `ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte` - file assertions (optional)\n\n**RunDiffTests signature** (R2.1):\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\nRuns each test as a named subtest, executes both binaries with identical inputs, applies normalizers in order to stdout/stderr of both, and compares outputs.\n\n**Additional utilities:**\n- `NormalizeFunc` - type alias for `func([]byte) []byte`\n- `TimestampNormalizer` - built-in normalizer for timestamp patterns\n- `ComposeNormalizers` - helper to chain multiple normalizers\n- `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string)` - compiles Go package and returns binary path (placed in t.TempDir())\n\n### SIGPIPE Handler Pattern: `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Path:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5419/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\nImplementation uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel (not `signal.Ignore`):\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\nMatches GNU coreutils behavior - exits with 0 when stdout/stderr is closed. Safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine)."}],"totalDurationMs":44933,"totalTokens":26831,"totalToolUseCount":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":601,"cache_read_input_tokens":24967,"output_tokens":1258,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":601},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":24967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":601,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":5,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
